WEBVTT

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.350
You're early today, huh Éclair?

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.040
É- Éclair? What's going on?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.380
Usually you come flying through here, saying you're going to be late for work!

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.710
I hope it doesn't start raining, too.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.820
I know, you must have stayed up all night, right?

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:22.720
Shall I get you a nice, strong <i>café</i> latte?

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:29.060
Sorry... make it tea. I have the day off.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:33.360
Well then, how about chamomile tea? It will relax you.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:43.500
Thanks for waiting.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.740
Thanks.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:55.620
Whoa there, you can't go taking sedatives with tea!

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:59.490
Sorry, Caprice.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.360
Come on in! Good morning!

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.920
Morning.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.780
<i>Again!</i>

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:28.010
Don't poke through too far in again, okay?

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.050
The usual way won't cut it this time...

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.650
We'll be fine, as long as the backups keep up.

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:36.990
Okay, the system has been suppressed.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:39.320
You're going to get left behind, Eclipse!

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.690
Eclipse? The chief!?

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:51.000
It's been half a year since I first looked upon your dirty faces here, rookies.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.670
There were those who ran away with their tails tucked between their legs,

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:58.010
but I can see that those of you who remain rather like it here.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:02.250
However, as you know, our National Planetary Federation

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.350
has been thrust into a state of war with the Planetary Republican Union,

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:06.020
Is that?

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:13.020
for three months now. Rookies, we can't afford to keep raising you here forever.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:14.390
Your training is finished.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:20.360
As of now, you are each appointed to your respective ranks.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:24.490
Finally, I will give you all one last order:

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.400
Don't go dying. That is all!

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.000
Let me out of here! Let me out!

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.130
If you let those guys get away with this,

00:06:57.130 --> 00:07:00.000
it will mean the deaths of hundreds of millions more people!

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.270
Why!? Why!?

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:15.350
It's the ordered time.

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:18.690
Aren't you going to fire?

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:23.560
I can't fire. Not of my own will.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:27.130
Hands up! Fists closed tightly!

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.930
It won't do any good.

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:36.770
It can't be!

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:43.040
It was set to fire before we even left Aineias.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:48.720
Aineias!? Then, this was the GOTT's doing?

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:53.150
Where is this?

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:58.330
Oh, dear, are you hungry?

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:02.230
You can touch me there, but I can't give you any milk!

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.240
Enough, already!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:31.920
Are you okay?

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.590
Were you having a bad dream?

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:40.760
I'm sorry...

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:46.700
Sorry, Caprice. It's my fault.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:50.310
What's this?

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:55.650
It's the tab I've run up until now.

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:58.280
What, does that mean you won't be coming again?

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.730
Éclair, you idiot! Don't ever come here again!

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:10.260
You idiot...

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:24.470
I guess there's no reason why these drugs would be meant for regular people.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:49.640
<i>Come to think of it, earlier...</i>

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:53.980
The red hair, the moves... you're Éclair, aren't you?

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:57.640
I don't know anything about my predecessor!

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:01.890
<i>"Predecessors..." "pre-holders..."</i>

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:06.620
<i>the people who had the code name "Éclair" before I did...</i>

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:22.340
"Predecessor"? "Pre-holder"? No, I'm not your "predecessor."

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:24.570
I'm...

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.680
I know that!

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:32.610
That you... are me...

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:34.480
That's right.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:38.090
You're the woman who, despite killing others countless times,

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:42.530
keeps clinging to life, no matter how many times you die.

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:49.630
"Predecessor"? You can't get away with pretending it's somebody else.

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:51.570
Your hands...

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.900
...are covered in blood!

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:10.610
Yes, this is Éclair...

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:40.350
Chief, Éclair has arrived.

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:42.110
Come in.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:53.700
Chief, um... Éclair is...

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:56.700
Thank you, Mercredi.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.960
Please excuse me.

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:10.050
It's me.

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:12.050
Ah, it's you...

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:15.450
This is Omega. The situation is moving forward.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.390
The current level is at e-flat.

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:20.090
We have secured 80°% of the scheduled data.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.730
Our coordinates have been forwarded.

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:24.090
We also got a sample of E-4.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:27.060
More importantly, the opposition are ES members.

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:29.900
I don't believe they are from the Pelias government,

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:33.000
but they aren't like any petty smuggling outfit either.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.010
Anyhow, more like watchdogs than counters.

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:38.340
Please move the schedule up by 620 counts.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:39.470
Out.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:46.680
Please help Un-ou and A-ou escape. Ordinarily, this special assignment...

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:53.020
...would go to Tweedledee and Tweedledum, but we have to hurry.

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:54.490
Understood.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:12.470
Understood.

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:21.580
I'm terribly sorry, but we must hurry along.

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:30.390
What's this?

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:35.000
If you're going to be protecting someone, take the.45.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.370
If you're going to be placing it against your own temple,

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.930
the 9mm will be more than enough.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.680
Planet Pelias is out in this frontier region.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.690
It does belong to the Global Union.

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:00.720
It's famous as being a Mecca of smuggling, huh?

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:05.030
Planetary governments outside of the Union call it a "Smuggling Heaven."

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.860
Which probably makes it that much more of a hell

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.030
for those two who went to investigate.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:11.800
Anyhow, they're planning to make a raid on detachments

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:14.370
in other smuggling footholds simultaneously,

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:17.740
but helping Un-ou and A-ou escape safely

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:20.380
and return with their data is our first priority.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:23.480
So we're peeking in through the mouth of hell, huh?

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:26.050
That must be fun for you, right <i>Éclair-san?</i>

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:27.740
Sure.

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:39.660
They're all pretty pissed off, huh?

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.670
You over-provoked them by dressing up as a woman.

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:47.670
Yeah, but did you see their faces? Even their ears were beet-red!

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:48.670
What's the matter?

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:51.200
I don't know! Our velocity!

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:58.350
We're caught in a force field. It's their ability!

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:01.810
Sheesh, I hate a man that doesn't know when to give up!

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:08.250
TP!

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:16.030
Dammit, what's wrong with the inertial drive!?

00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:18.700
Phase interference. It's ahead of us.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:20.700
Son of a bitch!

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:22.870
I understand how you must feel,

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:26.210
but you'd be better off if you stopped using that kind of language.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:40.660
I'm sorry I haven't seen you in some time.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:41.990
Lumiere!

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:42.990
Where's Éclair?

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:45.460
Well, she stopped off.

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:49.160
What's she!?

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:21.690
It's still not over!

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:28.370
One more shot!

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:31.040
Geez, that thing's as relentless as its master!

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:35.650
With its life-form homing, decoys and jamming won't work on it!

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:37.810
You son of a bitch!

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:43.420
Éclair!

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.520
Donner!

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.000
She couldn't be!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.010
Stop! Éclair!

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:04.700
Éclair!

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:23.550
Goodbye!

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.500
Éclair!

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:58.450
I told you that you couldn't escape from me, didn't I?

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:02.320
Think so?

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:26.780
Where am I?

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.800
Grandma, you dummy!

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.990
What's the matter?

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:05.330
Grandma said she was going to die. Is she really going to die?

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.150
When someone has accomplished

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:27.680
everything they have to do while they're still alive, they get sent for.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.690
Look at your grandma.

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:32.310
There isn't anything about her that's afraid, right?

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:38.290
But I want to have her live longer.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:41.960
Well then, stay with her some more.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:46.640
Everything that is born...

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:49.830
...dies at some time.

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:52.980
Including you...

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:54.770
...and me...

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:09.580
That's... pretty big talk, isn't it? As you ignore your own shortcomings?

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:12.660
You're right...

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:17.030
My hands may indeed be covered in blood, and at some point,

00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:20.660
I may become one of your group,

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:27.340
but right now, this life is mine. I'll do what I have to do,

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:31.680
until I'm content, like that person over there.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:36.290
You can say whatever you will, but I am you.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:39.350
I will always be at your side.

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:44.890
Yep. Keep watch over me, okay?

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:06.980
Do you not need these any longer?

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:10.710
If not, I will throw them away.

00:21:21.330 --> 00:21:23.090
Come on in!

00:21:31.340 --> 00:21:32.330
Welcome!

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:09.870
<i>Release from restriction.</i>

00:23:09.870 --> 00:23:12.880
<i>The moment one is set loose from heavy chains,</i>

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:15.250
<i>rigid freedom seizes upon them.</i>

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:19.510
<i>Next time on Kiddy Grade</i>
